    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Idioms are figurative expressions whose meanings cannot be deduced from their individual literal words.",
        "Large reference tables organize idioms systematically to aid structured memorization.",
        "Idiomatic usage is frequently tested in spot-the-error, sentence completion, and phrase replacement questions.",
        "Understanding the origin or context of an idiom significantly improves long-term recall."
      ],
      "id": "u56thc3"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Watch out for prepositional errors in idioms, as altering a single preposition can make the expression incorrect.",
        "Examiners often present literal interpretations as distractor options in multiple-choice questions.",
        "Focus on high-frequency idioms asked in previous years' SSC and Banking question papers."
      ],
      "id": "w1735r9"
    },
